cy is  aligned and pushing in the same  direction but i think actually our  global leadership is recognized the  international community is still well  short of the pledged hundred billion a  year  all of the reporting is that that's to  do with america not stepping up is that  the case from your point of view and  what can be done to change that this 100  billion goal was committed several years  ago and real progress has been made so  the last figures from 2018 showed that  we were at 78.9 billion a year  but let's be honest it's going to be  very hard for that to translate into 100  billion dollars a year by 2020. we are  pushing every single donor to deliver to  step up the uk we doubled our climate  finance so it's 11.6 billion pounds over  five years and we're expecting everybody  to do the same but america hasn't really  increased the amount that it's going to  pledge particularly for the size of its  economy what are you saying to your  counterparts at the u.s well they did  increase but we also know that they can  do more so we continue to to pressure  them to discuss with them what the  opportunities might be and we look  forward to hopefully some positive  signals in the weeks to come ahead of  cop26  and today the prime minister boris  johnson told the g20 to show the  leadership that the world needs to  tackle climate change he was speaking at  an economic and climate forum hosted by  the u.s president who called for global  action  without adequate commitments from every  nation in this room  the goal of limiting and warming to 1.5  degrees slips through our hands and  that's a disaster we have to bring to  glasgow our highest possible ambitions  those that have not yet done so time is  running now  meanwhile more than 70 people have been  arrested in climate protests on the m25  again today many of the demonstrators  described by the home secretary as  selfish had been released after blocking  the major motorway earlier this week  before then going on to cause more  disruption skies iva bennett has more  this was one of several locations the  demonstrators targeted this morning  either on or around the m25 here in  essex but also in kent and surrey also a  location near stanster airport on the  m11  the protesters tried to glue themselves  to the road blocking traffic on these  busy interchanges in one case also  pouring paint on the road trying to  cause disruption they're from a group  called insulate britain and they're  demanding the government does more to  make homes in britain more energy  efficient to do more to tackle climate  change it's the third time they've  demonstrated this week on the m25 what  was different this time around though  was the police response which was  noticeably swifter and also seemingly  more heavy-handed with the police  forcibly removing protesters from the  mood trying to from the road trying to  uh keep disruption to a minimum and that  followed comments from the home  secretary pretty patel  last night in which she branded their  protesters as selfish she said the  guerrilla tactics used by insulate  britain detract from their cause and i  know the public will agree that the  scenes on the m25 this week were  completely unacceptable the police have  our full support they must uphold the  law and take decisive action this kind  of disruption is dangerous and takes  police away from communities where they  are needed most so it seems the police  were following through on that warning  for their part the protesters have said  this kind of action won't stop until  their demands are met with some  demonstrators here today actually coming  straight from the custody center after  being released following their arrests  earlier in the week so if they're  prepared to do that i think this won't  be the last protest of this kind that we  see  well that's got a lot of people fired up  stay with us because we're going to be  discussing whether protests like the  ones we're seeing there 